From: Edo Tensei <edo-tensei@local>
Subject: [PATCH] ps2xRuntime: respeitar delaysNextBranchRead no loop rapido VU1

O loop rapido de VU1Interpreter::run gravava m_viBranchBackupValid para
qualquer escrita em VI (viWriteMask != 0), inclusive instrucoes cujo resultado
deve ser visivel imediatamente no branch seguinte (FMAND, FSAND, ILW, XTOP,
XITOP). Nos microprogramas de batalha (ex: 76548714fc26fb7a, f0eacbc321ec9dfc),
FMAND/FSAND seguido de IBNE/IBEQ lia o valor antigo de VI, quebrando culling e
shading dos personagens (cabecas/bracos/pernas pretos).

--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_core.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_core.cpp
@@ -2311,7 +2311,7 @@ void VU1Interpreter::run(uint8_t *vuCode, uint32_t codeSize,
             }
 
             m_viBranchBackupValid = false;
-            if (viWriteMask != 0u)
+            if (viWriteMask != 0u && decoded.lowerUsage.delaysNextBranchRead)
             {
                 m_viBranchBackupReg = writtenVi;
                 m_viBranchBackupValue = oldVi;
